Yes bro 👍 If you mean **Angular Service**, here is the **full simple method from creating the service → writing code → connecting it to component → running it**.

I'll use a simple **Student Service** because it matches your current program.

## 1. Create Angular project

If you already have your project, skip this.

```bash
ng new StudentService
cd StudentService
ng serve
```

Choose:

```text
CSS
SSR → No
```

---

## 2. Generate a service

Open terminal inside the project:

```bash
ng generate service student
```

Short form:

```bash
ng g s student
```

It creates:

```text
src/app/student.service.ts
src/app/student.service.spec.ts
```

You mainly use:

```text
student.service.ts
```

---

## 3. Write service code

Open:

```text
src/app/student.service.ts
```

Put:

```ts
import { Injectable } from '@angular/core';

@Injectable({
  providedIn: 'root'
})
export class StudentService {

  students: any[] = [];

  addStudent(student: any) {
    this.students.push(student);
  }

  getStudents() {
    return this.students;
  }

  deleteStudent(index: number) {
    this.students.splice(index, 1);
  }
}
```

### Easy meaning

```text
Service = stores common data and methods
```

Here the service stores the students and performs:

* Add
* Get
* Delete

---

# 4. Use service in Student Component

Open:

```text
student.component.ts
```

Use:

```ts
import { Component } from '@angular/core';
import { StudentService } from '../student.service';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-student',
  templateUrl: './student.component.html',
  styleUrls: ['./student.component.css']
})
export class StudentComponent {

  id = '';
  name = '';

  students: any[] = [];

  constructor(private service: StudentService) {
    this.students = this.service.getStudents();
  }

  addStudent() {

    const student = {
      id: this.id,
      name: this.name
    };

    this.service.addStudent(student);

    this.clear();
  }

  deleteStudent(index: number) {
    this.service.deleteStudent(index);
  }

  clear() {
    this.id = '';
    this.name = '';
  }
}
```

---

# 5. HTML

Open:

```text
student.component.html
```

Put:

```html
<div class="main">

  <div class="inputbox">

    <h2>Student Form</h2>

    <label>ID:</label>
    <input type="text" [(ngModel)]="id">

    <label>Name:</label>
    <input type="text" [(ngModel)]="name">

    <button (click)="addStudent()">Submit</button>

  </div>


  <div class="outputbox">

    <h2>Students</h2>

    <table border="1">

      <tr>
        <th>ID</th>
        <th>Name</th>
        <th>Action</th>
      </tr>

      <tr *ngFor="let student of students; let i = index">

        <td>{{ student.id }}</td>
        <td>{{ student.name }}</td>

        <td>
          <button (click)="deleteStudent(i)">Delete</button>
        </td>

      </tr>

    </table>

  </div>

</div>
```

