# ⭐ Exam method to remember

For **Angular Service**, remember only these steps:

### Step 1 — Generate

```bash
ng g s student
```

### Step 2 — Service

```ts
@Injectable({
  providedIn: 'root'
})
export class StudentService {

  students: any[] = [];

  addStudent(student: any) {
    this.students.push(student);
  }

  getStudents() {
    return this.students;
  }
}
```

### Step 3 — Import service

```ts
import { StudentService } from '../student.service';
```

### Step 4 — Constructor injection

```ts
constructor(private service: StudentService) {}
```

### Step 5 — Call service

```ts
this.service.addStudent(student);
```

### Step 6 — Display

```html
<tr *ngFor="let student of students">
```

**Main idea:**

```text
Component → Service → Data
```

The **component handles the UI**, while the **service handles shared data/logic**.
